 "notes": "Continuation of Table XV Part II(B) Tri and poly-lingualism. Subsidiary column headers on header pages of this part print 'Dogri.', 'Panjabi.', 'Kashmiri.' (leaf 266 adds letters (B),(C),(D)); recorded as Dogri/Panjabi/Kashmiri. Rows printed nil ('....') in every column are omitted; subsidiary triples all-nil are omitted. Remarks: wrapped lines joined; a word broken across lines ('langu-'/'ages.' or 'langu'/'ages.') is rejoined as 'languages.'. Page 262 (header page: TABLE XV.-PART II (B). TRI AND POLY-LINGUALISM. Jammu and Kashmir Census 1931; column heads Taluk, Mother-tongue, No. of Persons speaking Mother-tongue, No. of Persons speaking Subsidiary Languages: Dogri., Panjabi., Kashmiri.; Remarks). Top rows Panjabi..Shina complete the Uttarmachhipura Tehsil block (Kashmir North) from leaf 271. District printed 'Muzaffarabad District' (Part I name 'Muzaffarabad' used in area_path). Muzaffarabad Tehsil block continues on leaf 273 (Pothwari..Shina). Uttarmachhipura Panjabi row: Dogri Persons figure is an ink-filled blob whose outline (top flag) is that of a 5; read as 5, consistent with Males 5, Females nil and the remark (whose leading '5' is similarly blotted). Muzaffarabad Dogri Males '58' has a broken-type 5; 58+42=100. Rows all-nil omitted: Uttarmachhipura Chabhali, Pothwari, Shina; Uri Chabhali, Ladakhi, Shina; Muzaffarabad Chabhali."
